1
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:39,910
Most of us encounter chemicals in one form or another every day.
我们大多数人每天都会以这样或那样的形式接触到化学品。

2
00:00:39,910 --> 00:00:44,830
They're used in a wide range of products and laboratory processes, and are often essential
它们被用于各种各样的产品和实验室流程中，而且往往是

3
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:46,810
in our jobs.
我们工作中必不可少的。

4
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:51,910
But if we don't take the proper precautions, many chemicals can be hazardous to our safety
但如果我们不采取适当的预防措施，许多化学品就可能危害我们的安全

5
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:53,910
and health.
和健康。

6
00:00:53,910 --> 00:00:59,470
There are many types of potentially hazardous chemicals, flammables, corrosives, irritants,
潜在危险化学品有很多类型：易燃物、腐蚀性物质、刺激物、

7
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:05,070
sensitizers, toxins, even carcinogens, which can cause cancer.
致敏物、毒物，甚至还有会致癌的致癌物。

8
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:10,350
Each of these chemicals has its own set of hazards, required safety precautions, and recommended
每一种化学品都有各自的危害、必需的安全防范措施以及建议的

9
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:12,750
emergency procedures.
应急程序。

10
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:16,070
So how can we work with hazardous chemicals safely?
那么，我们怎样才能安全地使用危险化学品呢？

11
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:18,590
How should we handle and store them?
我们应该如何搬运和储存它们？

12
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:21,950
What personal protective equipment should we use?
我们应该使用哪些个人防护装备？

13
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:35,380
And what should we do in an emergency?
在紧急情况下我们又该怎么做？

14
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:42,380
For years, material safety data sheets, MSDSs, provided us with the answers to these questions.
多年来，物质安全数据表，也就是 MSDS，为我们提供了这些问题的答案。

15
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:48,100
MSDSs came about as part of OSHA's Hazard Communication Standard.
MSDS 是 OSHA 危害沟通标准的一部分。

16
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:53,620
This right-to-know regulation required chemical manufacturers and importers to give their customers
这项知情权法规要求化学品制造商和进口商，向客户提供

17
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:59,420
MSDSs for any potentially hazardous products that they supplied.
他们所供应的任何潜在危险产品的 MSDS。

18
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:04,560
But although certain types of information had to be included, OSHA did not require a standard
但是，虽然某些类型的信息必须包含在内，OSHA 并没有要求物质安全数据表

19
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:08,540
format for material safety data sheets.
采用统一的格式。

20
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:15,420
As a result, MSDSs ended up in a variety of forms, with data arranged in different ways.
结果，MSDS 形式五花八门，数据的编排方式也各不相同。

21
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:19,060
This often made it hard to find the information that you needed.
这常常让人很难找到所需的信息。

22
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:24,460
And in an emergency situation, this could cost valuable time.
而在紧急情况下，这可能会耽误宝贵的时间。

23
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:28,500
Another difficulty with many material safety data sheets was that they were written in
许多物质安全数据表的另一个难题是，它们是用

24
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:33,620
technical language, as if they were intended only for health and safety professionals.
专业术语写的，好像只是写给健康与安全专业人员看的。

25
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:38,920
However, many other types of people, such as firefighters, emergency medical technicians,
然而，许多其他类型的人，比如消防员、急救医疗技术员，

26
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:45,920
and laboratory workers like you, also need to be able to understand what MSDSs tell them.
以及像你这样的实验室工作人员，也需要能够看懂 MSDS 告诉他们的内容。

27
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:51,820
To address these problems, OSHA has adopted the Globally Harmonized System of Classification
为解决这些问题，OSHA 已将《全球化学品统一分类

28
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:57,140
and Labeling of Chemicals, GHS for short, into the HASCOM standard.
和标签制度》，简称 GHS，纳入危害沟通标准。

29
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:01,840
The GHS was developed by the United Nations so that workers anywhere in the world would
GHS 是由联合国制定的，目的是让世界上任何地方的工作人员

30
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:06,800
be able to understand the hazards that a chemical presents.
都能够理解一种化学品所带来的危害。

31
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:12,780
A major part of the Globally Harmonized System is the use of the GHS Safety Data Sheet.
全球统一制度的一个重要组成部分，是使用 GHS 安全技术说明书。

32
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:18,320
It gives chemical manufacturers a standard format and specific, understandable language to use
它为化学品制造商提供了统一的格式，以及具体易懂的语言，

33
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:21,100
to describe a chemical's hazards.
用来描述化学品的危害。

34
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:26,680
Although compliance with the GHS is voluntary, most industrialized countries are adopting it
虽然遵循 GHS 是自愿的，但大多数工业化国家都在采用它，

35
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:32,160
and will be starting to use GHS Safety Data Sheets soon, if they haven't already.
而且如果还没有用的话，很快也将开始使用 GHS 安全技术说明书。

36
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:38,540
So it also makes it easier for U.S. chemical companies to sell their products internationally.
所以它也让美国化学品公司更容易在国际上销售产品。

37
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:43,120
For many workers, the GHS Safety Data Sheet will look very familiar.
对许多工作人员来说，GHS 安全技术说明书看起来会非常眼熟。

38
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:47,600
That's because it's formatted almost exactly like one of the versions of the ANSI Material
这是因为它的格式几乎和 ANSI 物质安全数据表的某个版本

39
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:52,440
Safety Data Sheet, except for much of the information in Sections 2 and 3, whose
一模一样，只是第 2 部分和第 3 部分中的大部分信息

40
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:55,160
positions are swapped.
位置互换了。

41
00:03:55,160 --> 00:04:01,520
Although just like ANSI MSDS's, GHS Safety Data Sheets present information in an as-needed
不过，和 ANSI MSDS 一样，GHS 安全技术说明书也是按需要的先后

42
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:02,840
order.
顺序来呈现信息的。

43
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:08,280
The chemical's identity, its hazards and some emergency instructions are provided up front
化学品的标识、危害以及一些应急说明放在最前面，

44
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:11,200
for quick and easy access.
便于快速查阅。

45
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:17,480
Basic safety information is presented next in easy-to-understand language.
接下来用通俗易懂的语言介绍基本安全信息。

46
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:22,120
Supporting technical data, as well as information for health and safety professionals is provided
辅助性的技术数据，以及供健康与安全专业人员使用的信息，放在

47
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:26,000
later in the SDS.
安全技术说明书的后面。

48
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,620
Safety Data Sheets are designed to answer four basic questions that anyone who encounters
安全技术说明书旨在回答任何接触化学品的人可能有的

49
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:33,040
a chemical might have.
四个基本问题。

50
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:37,400
What is the material and what are its hazards?
这是什么物质，它有哪些危害？

51
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:42,800
What should I do if a problem occurs when I'm working with this material?
如果我在使用这种物质时出了问题，我该怎么做？

52
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:48,980
What precautions should I take to prevent problems when I work with this material?
使用这种物质时，我应该采取哪些预防措施来防止出问题？

53
00:04:48,980 --> 00:05:04,120
And finally, is there anything else I should know about this material?
最后，关于这种物质，还有什么我应该知道的吗？

54
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:10,080
Each of these questions is answered by one or more sections of the Safety Data Sheet.
每个问题都由安全技术说明书的一个或多个部分来回答。

55
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:15,960
For example, Sections 1, 2 and 3 provide answers to the first question, what is the material
例如，第 1、2、3 部分回答第一个问题：这是什么物质，

56
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:19,480
and what are its hazards?
它有哪些危害？

57
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:25,880
Section 1 of the SDS identifies the material using the standard GHS product identifier.
安全技术说明书的第 1 部分使用标准的 GHS 产品标识符来标识该物质。

58
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:32,160
You'll find the same product identifier on both the SDS and the chemical's container label.
你会在安全技术说明书和化学品的容器标签上看到相同的产品标识符。

59
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:37,640
Section 1 also lists the name, address and telephone number of the chemical's manufacturer,
第 1 部分还列出了化学品制造商、进口商或经销商的

60
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,440
